    "...or with the two digits swapped. Both would fit, so the puzzle would have two solutions.": {
      "comment": "Visual proof, Unique Rectangle: the swapped filling",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "...or with the two digits swapped. Both would fit, so the puzzle would have two solutions."
          }
        },
        "tr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "...ya da iki rakam yer değiştirerek. İkisi de uyardı, yani bulmacanın iki çözümü olurdu."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "3 Mistakes": {
      "comment": "Mistake limit option",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "3 Mistakes"
          }
        },
        "tr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "3 Hata"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "5 Mistakes": {
      "comment": "Mistake limit option",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "5 Mistakes"
          }
        },
        "tr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "5 Hata"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A cell's candidates are the digits not yet in its row, column or box. When only one candidate is left, that digit goes in the cell.": {
      "comment": "Technique guide (detailed hint explanation and training)",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A cell's candidates are the digits not yet in its row, column or box. When only one candidate is left, that digit goes in the cell."
          }
        },
        "tr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Bir hücrenin adayları, satırında, sütununda ve kutusunda henüz bulunmayan rakamlardır. Tek aday kaldığında o rakam hücreye gelir."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A chain of identical pairs": {
      "comment": "Technique subtitle: Remote Pair",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A chain of identical pairs"
          }
        },
        "tr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Uzak Çift"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A chain of two-candidate cells, each sharing a digit with the next. If the first cell isn't X, the chain forces the last cell to be X. So one of the two ends is X, and a cell that sees both can't be X.": {
      "comment": "Technique guide (detailed hint explanation and training)",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A chain of two-candidate cells, each sharing a digit with the next. If the first cell isn't X, the chain forces the last cell to be X. So one of the two ends is X, and a cell that sees both can't be X."
          }
        },
        "tr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Her biri bir sonrakiyle bir rakam paylaşan iki adaylı hücrelerden oluşan bir zincir. İlk hücre X değilse zincir son hücreyi X olmaya zorlar. Yani iki uçtan biri X'tir ve ikisini birden gören bir hücre X olamaz."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A chain on one digit alternates strong links (a house where the digit has exactly two spots) and weak links (two spots that see each other). If it starts and ends with a strong link, at least one of its ends holds the digit, so a cell that sees both ends can't.": {
      "comment": "Technique guide (detailed hint explanation and training)",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A chain on one digit alternates strong links (a house where the digit has exactly two spots) and weak links (two spots that see each other). If it starts and ends with a strong link, at least one of its ends holds the digit, so a cell that sees both ends can't."
          }
        },
        "tr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Tek rakamlı bir zincir güçlü bağlarla (rakamın tam iki yeri olduğu bir birim) zayıf bağları (birbirini gören iki yer) sırayla dizer. Zincir güçlü bir bağla başlayıp bitiyorsa uçlarından en az biri rakamı alır; bu yüzden iki ucu birden gören bir hücre alamaz."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A finned fish is an X-Wing or Swordfish with one or two extra cells, the fin, inside a single box. If the fin doesn't hold the digit, the fish works as usual; if it does, it rules out the cells it sees. Cells hit in both cases, in the fin's box and in the fish's columns, lose the digit.": {
      "comment": "Technique guide (detailed hint explanation and training)",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A finned fish is an X-Wing or Swordfish with one or two extra cells, the fin, inside a single box. If the fin doesn't hold the digit, the fish works as usual; if it does, it rules out the cells it sees. Cells hit in both cases, in the fin's box and in the fish's columns, lose the digit."
          }
        },
        "tr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Yüzgeçli balık, tek bir kutu içinde bir ya da iki fazla hücresi (yüzgeç) olan bir X-Wing ya da Swordfish'tir. Yüzgeç rakamı almıyorsa balık her zamanki gibi çalışır; alıyorsa gördüğü hücreleri eler. Her iki durumda da etkilenen hücreler, yani yüzgecin kutusunda ve balığın sütunlarında olanlar, rakamı kaybeder."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A pivot cell with two candidates, X and Y, sees two cells with XZ and YZ. Whatever the pivot holds, one of the two other cells becomes Z. So any cell that sees both of them can't be Z.": {
      "comment": "Technique guide (detailed hint explanation and training)",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A pivot cell with two candidates, X and Y, sees two cells with XZ and YZ. Whatever the pivot holds, one of the two other cells becomes Z. So any cell that sees both of them can't be Z."
          }
        },
        "tr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "İki adaylı (X ve Y) bir merkez hücre, XZ ve YZ adaylı iki hücreyi görür. Merkez ne olursa olsun, diğer iki hücreden biri Z olur. Bu yüzden ikisini birden gören hiçbir hücre Z olamaz."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A proper puzzle has exactly one solution. Four cells in two rows, two columns and two boxes that could all end up as only A or B would allow two solutions, since A and B could be swapped. So the solution must break the pattern, and depending on the other candidates in the corners, that rules out digits in the corners or around them.": {
      "comment": "Technique guide (detailed hint explanation and training)",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A proper puzzle has exactly one solution. Four cells in two rows, two columns and two boxes that could all end up as only A or B would allow two solutions, since A and B could be swapped. So the solution must break the pattern, and depending on the other candidates in the corners, that rules out digits in the corners or around them."
          }
        },
        "tr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Düzgün bir bulmacanın tam bir çözümü vardır. İki satır, iki sütun ve iki kutuya yayılan dört hücrenin hepsi yalnızca A ya da B olabilseydi, A ile B yer değiştirebileceği için iki çözüm olurdu. Bu yüzden çözüm bu deseni bozmak zorundadır; köşelerdeki diğer adaylara göre bu, köşelerde ya da çevrelerinde bazı rakamları eler."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A row and a column each have a digit in exactly two cells, and one cell of each pair sits in the same box. Those two can't both hold the digit, so at least one of the far ends does. A cell that sees both far ends can't hold it.": {
      "comment": "Technique guide (detailed hint explanation and training)",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A row and a column each have a digit in exactly two cells, and one cell of each pair sits in the same box. Those two can't both hold the digit, so at least one of the far ends does. A cell that sees both far ends can't hold it."
          }
        },
        "tr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Bir satır ve bir sütunun her birinde bir rakam tam iki hücreye girebiliyor ve her çiftin bir hücresi aynı kutuda. Bu ikisi birlikte rakamı alamaz, yani uzak uçlardan en az biri alır. İki uzak ucu birden gören bir hücre rakamı alamaz."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "About the Technique": {
      "comment": "Hint panel: opens the written guide",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
