            "value": "Hataları Sil"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Every %lld in one set sees every %lld in the other, so %lld is in at most one of them. The set without %lld has as many digits as cells left, so it must hold all of them, %lld included.": {
      "comment": "Hint walkthrough page: ALS-XZ, the restricted common digit",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Every %1$lld in one set sees every %2$lld in the other, so %3$lld is in at most one of them. The set without %4$lld has as many digits as cells left, so it must hold all of them, %5$lld included."
          }
        },
        "tr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Bir kümedeki her %1$lld diğer kümedeki her %2$lld adayını görüyor; yani %3$lld en fazla birinde olabilir. %4$lld olmayan kümede hücre sayısı kadar rakam kalır, bu yüzden hepsini almak zorundadır; %5$lld de dahil."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Every case rules it out, so %@ can be removed from the cells marked in red.": {
      "comment": "Visual proof conclusion: eliminations",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Every case rules it out, so %@ can be removed from the cells marked in red."
          }
        },
        "tr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Her durumda elendiği için %1$@ kırmızıyla işaretli hücrelerden silinebilir."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Every digit in its row, column and box rules itself out of the cell at %@.": {
      "comment": "Visual proof, Naked Single",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Every digit in its row, column and box rules itself out of the cell at %@."
          }
        },
        "tr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Satırındaki, sütunundaki ve kutusundaki her rakam kendini %1$@ hücresinden eler."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Every empty cell has exactly two candidates except the cell at %@, which has three.": {
      "comment": "Hint walkthrough page: BUG+1 position",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Every empty cell has exactly two candidates except the cell at %@, which has three."
          }
        },
        "tr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "%1$@ hücresi dışındaki tüm boş hücrelerin tam iki adayı var; bu hücrenin üç adayı var."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Every house needs each digit exactly once. If a digit has only one cell left in a house, because every other empty cell already sees that digit, it must go there, even if the cell itself still has other candidates.": {
      "comment": "Technique guide (detailed hint explanation and training)",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Every house needs each digit exactly once. If a digit has only one cell left in a house, because every other empty cell already sees that digit, it must go there, even if the cell itself still has other candidates."
          }
        },
        "tr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Her birimde her rakam tam bir kez bulunur. Bir rakamın bir birimde girebileceği tek hücre kaldıysa (diğer tüm boş hücreler o rakamı zaten görüyorsa), hücrenin başka adayları olsa bile rakam oraya gelir."
          }
        }
      }
    },
