    "So %@ can't go in the cells marked in red.": {
      "comment": "Hint walkthrough page: what an elimination rules out, before the step it leads to",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "So %@ can't go in the cells marked in red."
          }
        },
        "tr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Yani %@ kırmızıyla işaretli hücrelere giremez."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "So %@ can't go in the cells marked in red. No digit can be placed from this alone yet; apply it and the next hint continues from here.": {
      "comment": "Hint result for an elimination that doesn't lead to a placement within a few steps",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "So %@ can't go in the cells marked in red. No digit can be placed from this alone yet; apply it and the next hint continues from here."
          }
        },
        "tr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Yani %@ kırmızıyla işaretli hücrelere giremez. Bundan tek başına henüz bir rakam yerleştirilemiyor; uygularsan sonraki ipucu buradan devam eder."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "So %lld goes in the cell at %@.": {
      "comment": "Visual proof conclusion: placement",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "So %1$lld goes in the cell at %2$@."
          }
        },
        "tr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Yani %2$@ hücresine %1$lld gelir."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "So %lld is at %@ or at %@, and a cell that sees both can't be %lld.": {
      "comment": "Hint walkthrough page: chain conclusion when both ends are the same digit",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "So %1$lld is at %2$@ or at %3$@, and a cell that sees both can't be %4$lld."
          }
        },
        "tr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Yani %1$lld ya %2$@ ya da %3$@ hücresinde; ikisini birden gören bir hücre %4$lld olamaz."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "So %lld is in at least one of the two sets, and a cell that sees every %lld in both can't be %lld.": {
      "comment": "Hint walkthrough page: ALS-XZ conclusion",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "So %1$lld is in at least one of the two sets, and a cell that sees every %2$lld in both can't be %3$lld."
          }
        },
        "tr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Yani %1$lld iki kümeden en az birinde; iki kümedeki her %2$lld adayını gören bir hücre %3$lld olamaz."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "So %lld is in one of the cells marked in green.": {
      "comment": "Visual proof: the digit is somewhere among the green cells",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "So %lld is in one of the cells marked in green."
          }
        },
        "tr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Yani %1$lld yeşille işaretli hücrelerden birinde."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "So %lld is on one of the two diagonals of the highlighted rectangle. Either way %@ and %@ each get a %lld here, so it can be removed from the rest of them.": {
      "comment": "Hint walkthrough page: X-Wing, conclusion",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "So %1$lld is on one of the two diagonals of the highlighted rectangle. Either way %2$@ and %3$@ each get a %4$lld here, so it can be removed from the rest of them."
          }
        },
        "tr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Yani %1$lld işaretli dikdörtgenin iki köşegeninden birinde. Her iki durumda da %2$@ ve %3$@ burada birer %4$lld alır; bu yüzden bu çizgilerin geri kalanından silinebilir."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "So at least one of the other two ends, %@ or %@, is %lld. A cell that sees both can't be %lld.": {
      "comment": "Hint walkthrough page: Skyscraper and 2-String Kite, conclusion",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "So at least one of the other two ends, %1$@ or %2$@, is %3$lld. A cell that sees both can't be %4$lld."
          }
        },
        "tr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Yani diğer iki uçtan en az biri, %1$@ ya da %2$@, %3$lld olmalı. İkisini birden gören bir hücre %4$lld olamaz."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "So inside %@, %lld is on %@.": {
      "comment": "Visual proof, Empty Rectangle: box, digit, kept line",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "So inside %1$@, %2$lld is on %3$@."
          }
        },
        "tr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Yani %1$@ içinde %2$lld, %3$@ üzerindedir."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "So the cell at %@ is %lld or %lld, and its other candidates can be removed.": {
      "comment": "Hint walkthrough page: chain conclusion when both ends are in one cell",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "So the cell at %1$@ is %2$lld or %3$lld, and its other candidates can be removed."
          }
        },
        "tr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Yani %1$@ hücresi %2$lld ya da %3$lld; diğer adayları silinebilir."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "So the cell at %@ is %lld or the cell at %@ is %lld. They see each other, so the cell at %@ can't be %@.": {
      "comment": "Hint walkthrough page: chain conclusion with different digits, one elimination",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "So the cell at %1$@ is %2$lld or the cell at %3$@ is %4$lld. They see each other, so the cell at %5$@ can't be %6$@."
          }
        },
        "tr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Yani %1$@ hücresi %2$lld ya da %3$@ hücresi %4$lld. Bu hücreler birbirini görüyor; bu yüzden %5$@ hücresi %6$@ olamaz."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "So the cell at %@ is %lld or the cell at %@ is %lld. They see each other, so the first can't be %lld and the second can't be %lld.": {
      "comment": "Hint walkthrough page: chain conclusion when the ends are different digits in cells that see each other",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "So the cell at %1$@ is %2$lld or the cell at %3$@ is %4$lld. They see each other, so the first can't be %5$lld and the second can't be %6$lld."
          }
        },
        "tr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Yani %1$@ hücresi %2$lld ya da %3$@ hücresi %4$lld. Bu hücreler birbirini görüyor; bu yüzden ilki %5$lld, ikincisi %6$lld olamaz."
          }
        }
      }
    },
