            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Two digits, two cells"
          }
        },
        "tr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Gizli İkili"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Two links sharing a base": {
      "comment": "Technique subtitle",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Two links sharing a base"
          }
        },
        "tr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Gökdelen"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Two of these cells are in %@, so they can't both be %lld.": {
      "comment": "Hint walkthrough page: Skyscraper and 2-String Kite, the connection",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Two of these cells are in %1$@, so they can't both be %2$lld."
          }
        },
        "tr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Bu hücrelerden ikisi %1$@ içinde, yani ikisi birden %2$lld olamaz."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Two rows each have a digit in exactly two cells, and one end of each pair is in the same column. Those two ends see each other, so at most one of them holds the digit, which means at least one of the other two ends does. A cell that sees both of those ends can't hold it.": {
      "comment": "Technique guide (detailed hint explanation and training)",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Two rows each have a digit in exactly two cells, and one end of each pair is in the same column. Those two ends see each other, so at most one of them holds the digit, which means at least one of the other two ends does. A cell that sees both of those ends can't hold it."
          }
        },
        "tr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "İki satırın her birinde bir rakam tam iki hücreye girebiliyor ve her çiftin bir ucu aynı sütunda. Bu iki uç birbirini görür, yani en fazla biri rakamı alır; bu da diğer iki uçtan en az birinin aldığı anlamına gelir. Bu iki ucu birden gören bir hücre rakamı alamaz."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Typical Time": {
      "comment": "Pause screen: estimated time for a typical player",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Typical Time"
          }
        },
        "tr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Tahmini Süre"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Undo": {
      "comment": "Button that undoes the last action",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Undo"
          }
        },
        "tr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Geri Al"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Undo Last Mistake": {
      "comment": "Result sheet after a loss: takes back the last mistake and plays on.",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Undo Last Mistake"
          }
        },
        "tr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Son Hatayı Geri Al"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Undo it and look again, or ask for a hint.": {
      "comment": "Practice: after a wrong move",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Undo it and look again, or ask for a hint."
          }
        },
        "tr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Geri al ve tekrar bak ya da ipucu iste."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Well done!": {
      "comment": "Practice: position solved",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Well done!"
          }
        },
        "tr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Aferin!"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "When a box's candidates for a digit all lie on one row and one column of the box, the box's copy of that digit is on that row or on that column. Combined with a house elsewhere where the digit has only two spots, this rules out the cell where both possibilities meet.": {
      "comment": "Technique guide (detailed hint explanation and training)",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "When a box's candidates for a digit all lie on one row and one column of the box, the box's copy of that digit is on that row or on that column. Combined with a house elsewhere where the digit has only two spots, this rules out the cell where both possibilities meet."
          }
        },
        "tr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Bir kutuda bir rakamın tüm adayları kutunun bir satırında ve bir sütununda duruyorsa, kutunun o rakamı ya o satırda ya da o sütundadır. Başka bir yerde rakamın yalnızca iki yeri olan bir birimle birleşince, iki olasılığın buluştuğu hücre elenir."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "When a row, column or box has only one empty cell left, that cell gets the one digit the house is still missing.": {
      "comment": "Technique guide (detailed hint explanation and training)",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "When a row, column or box has only one empty cell left, that cell gets the one digit the house is still missing."
          }
        },
        "tr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Bir satır, sütun ya da kutuda tek bir boş hücre kaldığında, o hücreye birimde eksik olan tek rakam gelir."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "When nothing simpler works, follow pairs and two-note cells and see where an assumption leads.": {
      "comment": "Technique guide (detailed hint explanation and training)",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "When nothing simpler works, follow pairs and two-note cells and see where an assumption leads."
          }
        },
        "tr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Daha basit hiçbir şey işe yaramadığında çiftleri ve iki notlu hücreleri izle ve bir varsayımın nereye götürdüğüne bak."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Whichever of them is %lld, the cell it sees can't be %lld and must be %lld. So one of the two cells is %lld, and a cell that sees both can't be %lld.": {
      "comment": "Hint walkthrough page: W-Wing, conclusion",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Whichever of them is %1$lld, the cell it sees can't be %2$lld and must be %3$lld. So one of the two cells is %4$lld, and a cell that sees both can't be %5$lld."
          }
        },
        "tr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Hangisi %1$lld olursa, gördüğü hücre %2$lld olamaz ve %3$lld olmak zorunda. Yani iki hücreden biri %4$lld; ikisini birden gören bir hücre %5$lld olamaz."
          }
        }
      }
    },
